WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.002
Previously on Love Live!

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:05.589
Thanks to our efforts at the open campus,
the school will not close just yet.

00:00:05.589 --> 00:00:09.384
We also learned that Minami-san has
been working at a maid cafe in Akiba.

00:00:09.384 --> 00:00:13.388
Unlike Honoka-chan and Umi-chan,
there's nothing really special about me.

00:00:13.388 --> 00:00:17.726
We had the downtrodden Minami-san write
Akiba-themed lyrics to help change herself.

00:00:17.726 --> 00:00:20.854
Coming to this place shows me
wonders and gives me courage.

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:22.939
Well there ya go, Kotori-chan!

00:00:22.939 --> 00:00:26.109
Take those words you just said and
mash 'em together to make song lyrics!

00:00:26.109 --> 00:00:28.320
Our street performance in Akiba
was a huge success.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:29.988
We will perform at Love Live!

00:00:32.574 --> 00:00:34.200
It's an inferno...

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:35.910
Yeah...

00:00:36.077 --> 00:00:39.873
This is incredibly stupid.
Why would we practice in this heat!?

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:42.834
Don't be like that. Let's just
hurry up and get practicing.

00:00:42.834 --> 00:00:44.044
O-Okay...

00:00:45.128 --> 00:00:49.215
Hanayo, please stop thinking of us
as your upperclassmen, okay?

00:00:49.966 --> 00:00:50.884
Okay.

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:53.261
Oh, I know! Let's all go on a trip together!

00:00:53.261 --> 00:00:55.597
Huh? Where'd that idea come from?

00:00:55.597 --> 00:00:59.517
Jeez, why didn't I think up such
an awesome plan sooner!?

00:00:59.517 --> 00:01:02.687
Like, a club trip? Could be fun!

00:01:02.687 --> 00:01:07.817
I agree. Besides, practicing every day
in such intense heat takes its toll.

00:01:07.817 --> 00:01:09.361
But where would we go?

00:01:09.527 --> 00:01:11.655
The beach, duh! It's summer.

00:01:11.655 --> 00:01:13.865
And how will we pay for this excursion?

00:01:13.865 --> 00:01:15.075
Oh, uh...

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:20.664
Kotori-chan, when's your
next paycheck coming?

00:01:20.664 --> 00:01:21.331
Huh?

00:01:21.706 --> 00:01:24.250
You expect poor Kotori to foot
the entire group's bill?

00:01:24.459 --> 00:01:27.671
Nah, I was just gonna borrow a teensy bit...

00:01:28.129 --> 00:01:31.424
Wait! Maki-chan, you're rich, so I bet
your family has a beach house!

00:01:32.008 --> 00:01:33.134
Yeah, we do.

00:01:34.469 --> 00:01:35.261
Really?

00:01:35.553 --> 00:01:37.430
Maki-chan, please!

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:39.891
Stop it. Why are you pestering me?

00:01:40.058 --> 00:01:43.228
She's right. We can't impose
on her family like that.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:46.314
Yeah... You're right...

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:55.198
Fine, fine. I'll ask my parents.

00:01:55.365 --> 00:01:57.450
- You willl?
- All right!

00:01:59.244 --> 00:02:00.161
Oh, yeah.

00:02:01.079 --> 00:02:04.249
This is as good a time as any for that, right?

00:02:04.249 --> 00:02:05.542
Huh?

00:02:19.681 --> 00:02:24.769
<i>Massugu ha omoi ga minna wo musubu Our honest
feelings are what will fie us all together.</i>

00:02:24.769 --> 00:02:29.607
Honki demo bukiyou butsukari au kokoro Even with
our clumsy sincerity, our hearts will still collide.

00:02:29.607 --> 00:02:34.446
Sore demo mitaiyo ohkina yume wa And despite
it all, we want to dream a really grand dream.

00:02:34.446 --> 00:02:39.033
Koko ni aruyo hajimatta bakari That dream
is here, and it has only now just begun!

00:02:39.033 --> 00:02:40.076
(wakatteru)
(We understand)

00:02:40.076 --> 00:02:43.997
Tanoshii dakejanai tamesarerudarou That it's not
all fun and games— we'll face a lot of obstacles.

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:44.956
(wakatteru)
(We understand)

00:02:44.956 --> 00:02:48.793
Datte sono kurushisa mo mirai That those
hardships will be paving our futures...

00:02:48.793 --> 00:02:49.836
ikundayo
So here we go!

00:02:49.836 --> 00:02:53.965
Atsumattara tsuyoi jibun ni nattekuyo If we all
join together, we'll be able to become stronger.

00:02:53.965 --> 00:02:58.595
(Kittone) kawari tsuzukete (WE'LL BE A STARY/) (We're sure
that) we will all grow and mature. (We'll become stars!)

00:02:58.595 --> 00:03:03.600
Sorezore ga sukina koto de ganbarerunara That's why we feel
that if we give the things that we love the most our all,

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:08.271
atarashii (basho ga) gohru dane what awaits
then (our new place) will be our goal.

00:03:08.271 --> 00:03:13.443
Sorezore no sukina koto wo shinjiteireba That's why we
feel that if we believe in the things we love in our lives,

00:03:13.443 --> 00:03:18.406
tokimeki wo (daite) susumerudarou we can learn to
love (then embrace) our butterflies and advance!

00:03:18.406 --> 00:03:23.870
(kowagaru kuse wa sutechae) tobikiri no egao de So crumple up your
fears, throw them away, and then just put on your brightest smiles!

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:31.461
(tonde tonde takaku) bokura wa ima no naka de (Higher and higher
we"ll fly) The lights that are shining within our hearts...

00:03:32.837 --> 00:03:36.216
kagayaki wo matteta
They're waiting to brighten the world.

00:03:41.763 --> 00:03:43.431
Marunouchi North Exit
What?

00:03:44.098 --> 00:03:45.809
No "-senpai" allowed?

00:03:45.809 --> 00:03:48.353
#10 - No Senpai Allowed!
It's been bothering me for a while now.

00:03:48.353 --> 00:03:52.398
School year-based honorifics are
important, but while we're a group,

00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:54.734
we can't get caught up in those formalities.

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:59.989
That's a good point. Sometimes I'll end up
following a third year just because it's natural.

00:03:59.989 --> 00:04:02.367
I don't remember getting treated like that.

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:06.496
Probably because you don't
feel like our upperclassman.

00:04:06.496 --> 00:04:08.540
If I'm not your senior, then what am [!?

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:09.791
Well...

00:04:09.791 --> 00:04:10.875
An underclassman?

00:04:11.334 --> 00:04:12.752
Someone's kid?

00:04:12.961 --> 00:04:15.088
I thought you were a child mascot.

00:04:15.088 --> 00:04:16.840
What do you see when you look at me!?

00:04:17.215 --> 00:04:21.094
Let's start the honorific-ignoring
experiment now, Honoka.

00:04:21.094 --> 00:04:23.763
Sure, sounds good to me...

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:28.351
Eli-chan!

00:04:32.355 --> 00:04:33.982
It kinda makes me jittery.

00:04:33.982 --> 00:04:35.692
I want to try it, too.

00:04:38.278 --> 00:04:40.446
Kotori...chan?

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:45.493
Yep, let's work hard together, Rin-chan.
The same goes for you, Maki-chan.

00:04:45.493 --> 00:04:47.745
Huh? Uh...

00:04:49.956 --> 00:04:54.127
Th-There's no reason for me to say
anyone's name right now, is there?

00:04:55.253 --> 00:04:59.465
Well, all right. The time has come to
depart for our overnight adventure!

00:04:59.465 --> 00:05:01.551
President Yazawa-san, the floor is yours.

00:05:01.551 --> 00:05:03.887
What? Who, me?

00:05:05.722 --> 00:05:07.223
Uh, um...

00:05:08.182 --> 00:05:10.310
VW.. . We...

00:05:11.019 --> 00:05:13.229
We embark!

00:05:15.356 --> 00:05:16.190
That's it?

00:05:16.190 --> 00:05:18.318
Not like I prepared a speech for this!

00:05:23.531 --> 00:05:25.491
This place is amazing, Maki-chan!

00:05:25.491 --> 00:05:27.785
The rich really know how to live!

00:05:27.785 --> 00:05:30.121
You think? It's ordinary to my eyes.

00:05:35.043 --> 00:05:36.794
Dibs on this bed!

00:05:39.005 --> 00:05:42.216
It's crazy big and soft!

00:05:42.216 --> 00:05:43.885
I'll curl up right here!

00:05:44.218 --> 00:05:46.804
Umi-senpai, you'd better pick a bed soon, too.

00:05:47.972 --> 00:05:49.223
Let's try that again.

00:05:49.557 --> 00:05:51.643
Right! Umi-chan.

00:05:51.643 --> 00:05:52.560
Honoka-chan.

00:05:53.519 --> 00:05:54.520
Asleep already!?

00:05:55.104 --> 00:05:57.065
You have a personal chef!?

00:05:57.815 --> 00:05:59.442
Is that surprising or something?

00:05:59.442 --> 00:06:03.696
Of course it is! Having someone like
that working in your home...

00:06:03.696 --> 00:06:05.365
It's really neat, huh?

00:06:05.365 --> 00:06:10.244
R-Really, now? So your house
is like this too, huh...?

00:06:10.244 --> 00:06:14.207
It goes without saying, but I have
a personal chef, as well.

00:06:14.207 --> 00:06:18.211
That's why I've never cooked
before in my entire life.

00:06:18.586 --> 00:06:22.173
Wow, you too, Nico-senpai?

00:06:22.173 --> 00:06:23.508
You mean "Nico-Ni."

00:06:23.508 --> 00:06:24.050
What?

00:06:24.050 --> 00:06:27.095
Don't call me Nico-senpai! It's Nico-Ni now.

00:06:27.428 --> 00:06:30.139
We could easily practice here.

00:06:30.139 --> 00:06:31.307
We could.

00:06:31.683 --> 00:06:35.395
But since we're at the beach,
why not enjoy the outdoors?

00:06:35.395 --> 00:06:40.400
I know where we are, but won't we bother
others if we raise too much of a ruckus?

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:43.236
You wanted to practice singing here, too?

00:06:43.236 --> 00:06:49.158
Naturally. We have less than a month
before the Love Live lineup is decided.

00:06:49.492 --> 00:06:51.577
Motivated, aren't we?

00:06:51.953 --> 00:06:55.164
So Hanayo-chan, why are you
lingering at the edge of the room?

00:06:55.498 --> 00:06:58.334
Large, open rooms make me uncomfortable.

00:06:59.585 --> 00:07:03.172
This is our practice itinerary
for while we're here.

00:07:04.507 --> 00:07:07.343
Wow, looks really intense...

00:07:09.387 --> 00:07:10.555
Umi, beach, when!?

00:07:11.723 --> 00:07:13.141
Excuse me?

00:07:13.141 --> 00:07:17.103
Y'know, the ocean!
Sandy beaches! Swimming!

00:07:17.103 --> 00:07:19.981
Oh, right, that. I wrote that in here, see?

00:07:19.981 --> 00:07:20.898
Swimming Running

00:07:20.898 --> 00:07:23.026
A ten-kilometer swim...

00:07:23.026 --> 00:07:25.486
Followed by ten kilometers of running?

00:07:26.029 --> 00:07:29.824
We've been slacking on our
physical stamina training.

00:07:29.824 --> 00:07:34.495
So, since we've come all this way,
I figured it was a prime opportunity!

00:07:34.495 --> 00:07:38.583
You're right about its importance, but I
wonder if everyone can handle it...

00:07:38.583 --> 00:07:41.502
Everything will be fine with a
burning passion in our hearts!

00:07:41.919 --> 00:07:45.048
Her motivation is so intense, it's creepy.

00:07:45.048 --> 00:07:46.299
Deal with her.

00:07:46.299 --> 00:07:48.051
Um, okay.

00:07:48.051 --> 00:07:48.926
Rin-chan!

00:07:48.926 --> 00:07:49.969
Got it.

00:07:51.804 --> 00:07:53.681
Umi-chan, look over there!

00:07:53.681 --> 00:07:55.016
Huh? What is it?

00:07:55.391 --> 00:07:57.810
- Now!
- Escape!

00:07:57.810 --> 00:08:00.688
No, wait!

00:08:00.688 --> 00:08:02.356
Seems a decision has been reached.

00:08:02.857 --> 00:08:05.818
What? Are you sure about this, Eli-senpai?

00:08:07.612 --> 00:08:09.405
That terminology is prohibited.

00:08:09.739 --> 00:08:11.032
I'm sorry.

00:08:11.032 --> 00:08:15.161
M's has been practicing hard
pretty much nonstop.

00:08:15.161 --> 00:08:20.625
It's just as important that we play together
and work to break down the age barrier.

00:08:22.710 --> 00:08:24.087
Hey!

00:08:24.087 --> 00:08:27.673
Umi-chan, Eli-chan!

00:08:28.091 --> 00:08:29.175
Okay!

00:08:29.634 --> 00:08:32.929
Come on, Umi. Let's go play.

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:36.891
Hurry it up, already!

00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:37.975
Over here!

00:08:53.699 --> 00:08:56.619
P-Please put that thing
away, Nozomi-senpai!

00:08:58.496 --> 00:08:59.997
Nozomi!

00:09:03.167 --> 00:09:04.210
You can do it!

00:09:04.502 --> 00:09:05.711
Nice, nice.

00:09:11.384 --> 00:09:13.678
They're the cutest things ever, huh?

00:09:13.678 --> 00:09:15.304
That's so like you, Nico.

00:09:18.558 --> 00:09:24.313
I know it's for the PV, but acting like
an impish girl all the time is so tiring.

00:09:24.313 --> 00:09:25.898
Sure.

00:09:25.898 --> 00:09:27.859
Mind if I sit here with you?

00:09:27.859 --> 00:09:28.985
Sure.

00:09:29.902 --> 00:09:30.987
Pardon me, then.

00:09:41.581 --> 00:09:43.082
A little more...

00:09:43.624 --> 00:09:45.209
Sorry, Nico-chan!

00:09:45.543 --> 00:09:47.753
Go throw your ball somewhere else!

00:09:47.753 --> 00:09:49.755
Nico-chan, you come play, too!

00:09:49.755 --> 00:09:52.717
As if I'd engage in something so childish.

00:09:52.717 --> 00:09:55.803
So you say, but I bet you just suck at it.

00:09:55.803 --> 00:09:57.471
What was that!?

00:09:57.471 --> 00:10:01.017
- Just you wait! Suffer my Love Nico Attack!
- Maki-chan, will you join us, too?

00:10:01.309 --> 00:10:03.811
What? I'm fine right here.

00:10:04.604 --> 00:10:06.314
I see.

00:10:06.314 --> 00:10:08.900
Maki's hard to get a gauge on, isn't she?

00:10:11.277 --> 00:10:12.820
Is it something I said?

00:10:14.071 --> 00:10:15.239
Not really.

00:10:16.908 --> 00:10:17.950
Going shopping?

00:10:17.950 --> 00:10:21.329
Apparently, the closest supermarket
is a long walk from here.

00:10:21.329 --> 00:10:23.164
Lemme go, too!

00:10:23.164 --> 00:10:26.417
It's fine. I can go by myself.

00:10:26.417 --> 00:10:28.377
Oh, you will...?

00:10:28.377 --> 00:10:31.672
Not like any of you know where the store is.

00:10:31.672 --> 00:10:33.424
Allow me to join you, then.

00:10:33.758 --> 00:10:34.717
What?

00:10:35.676 --> 00:10:39.180
Unless you dislike the idea of spending
some time with me, that is.

00:10:44.936 --> 00:10:47.188
What a gorgeous sunset.

00:10:48.064 --> 00:10:49.357
What're you up to?

00:10:49.357 --> 00:10:53.945
Nothing bad. I just thought you're
a troublesome sort, too.

00:10:55.321 --> 00:10:59.951
The type who wishes to be closer to others,
but has trouble expressing her feelings.

00:11:00.701 --> 00:11:03.037
This is how I normally behave.

00:11:03.037 --> 00:11:04.288
Right, right.

00:11:05.331 --> 00:11:08.042
Like I said, trouble expressing her feelings.

00:11:08.960 --> 00:11:12.171
Well, I mean, what do you want me to say?

00:11:15.466 --> 00:11:17.134
Oh, I just can't leave you alone.

00:11:17.134 --> 00:11:20.638
I'm well-acquainted with
someone a lot like you.

00:11:21.806 --> 00:11:22.974
What're you babbling about?

00:11:23.432 --> 00:11:27.103
It might be good for you to let loose
and have fun once in a while.

00:11:27.103 --> 00:11:28.688
This is a sleepover, after all.

00:11:35.236 --> 00:11:36.612
Love Live!

00:11:38.781 --> 00:11:40.700
You're all completely hopeless!

00:11:44.203 --> 00:11:49.667
I'm so sorry. I was doing my best to cook,
but everything was taking me so long...

00:11:56.465 --> 00:11:59.677
H-Hanayo, why are you the only
one with her rice on the side?

00:11:59.677 --> 00:12:01.095
Don't worry about that.

00:12:01.095 --> 00:12:03.556
Nico-chan, you're a pretty good cook.

00:12:05.349 --> 00:12:10.354
But wait... This afternoon, I thought you
said you'd never cooked before...?

00:12:11.147 --> 00:12:15.526
Yeah. You claimed your personal
chef always made your meals.

00:12:16.777 --> 00:12:21.365
Golly! This crazy thing is way too
heavy for my dainty arms...!

00:12:22.700 --> 00:12:26.787
M-Maybe you're going a bit too far now...

00:12:26.787 --> 00:12:31.625
Idols these days won't be able to make it
big if they can't cook a simple meal or two!

00:12:31.625 --> 00:12:32.835
You're flip-flopping!

00:12:34.795 --> 00:12:36.422
And I'm stuffed.

00:12:36.922 --> 00:12:39.550
You'll turn into a cow if you lie
down immediately after eating.

00:12:39.800 --> 00:12:42.887
Jeez, you really sound like
my mom sometimes...

00:12:42.887 --> 00:12:45.598
All right! Let's set off some fireworks!

00:12:45.598 --> 00:12:48.976
We should clean up before we do that.

00:12:49.352 --> 00:12:52.938
Oh! Leave that to me.
You all go on ahead, okay?

00:12:53.272 --> 00:12:54.482
Huh? But...

00:12:54.482 --> 00:12:58.277
"But" is right. We should all
pull our own weight.

00:12:58.277 --> 00:13:01.405
Let's all clean our own dishes.

00:13:01.405 --> 00:13:03.824
Besides, we should practice,
not set off fireworks.

00:13:04.200 --> 00:13:05.701
What? Now?

00:13:05.701 --> 00:13:10.247
Of course, since we whittled away
the entire afternoon playing.

00:13:10.247 --> 00:13:13.501
This doesn't feel like the right time, though...

00:13:13.501 --> 00:13:15.711
Especially for Honoka-chan...

00:13:15.711 --> 00:13:18.547
Yukiho, didja make the tea yet...?

00:13:18.547 --> 00:13:19.423
You're not at home!

00:13:20.049 --> 00:13:22.968
I'm going straight to bed after we clean up.

00:13:22.968 --> 00:13:26.389
Aw, c'mon, Maki-chan.
Set off fireworks with us.

00:13:26.389 --> 00:13:28.349
No fireworks. Practice.

00:13:28.349 --> 00:13:29.308
Seriously?

00:13:29.809 --> 00:13:32.770
Right!? I wanna play with fireworks tonight.

00:13:32.770 --> 00:13:34.730
I won't allow it.

00:13:34.730 --> 00:13:36.399
Kayo-chin, what do you think?

00:13:36.399 --> 00:13:39.527
W-Well, I want to take a bath...

00:13:39.527 --> 00:13:42.196
Giving us a third option doesn't
help matters, y"know?

00:13:42.196 --> 00:13:45.241
Yukiho, tea...

00:13:45.991 --> 00:13:48.452
- Maybe we should just rest.
- Tea...!

00:13:48.786 --> 00:13:50.704
We're all tired, aren't we?

00:13:51.205 --> 00:13:56.210
We can practice tomorrow morning
and set off fireworks tomorrow night.

00:13:56.502 --> 00:13:59.088
- Oh, okay. That works for me.
- Tea! Teal

00:13:59.088 --> 00:14:03.384
- Practice may prove more effective that way.
- Tea me! Tea me!

00:14:03.384 --> 00:14:05.594
The matter is settled.

00:14:09.306 --> 00:14:11.183
Now this feels good.

00:14:11.183 --> 00:14:12.518
Yep.

00:14:12.518 --> 00:14:15.104
We are absolutely going to
practice in the morning.

00:14:15.104 --> 00:14:17.356
Yeah, we heard you already.

00:14:17.356 --> 00:14:21.318
It's the first time we've all
bathed together like this.

00:14:21.318 --> 00:14:22.945
It's a real honor.

00:14:22.945 --> 00:14:25.573
Hanayo, you sound far too formal.

00:14:25.573 --> 00:14:27.491
Oh, excuse—

00:14:27.491 --> 00:14:28.200
Sorry.

00:14:29.577 --> 00:14:30.619
That's better.

00:14:35.499 --> 00:14:37.168
Ready, go!

00:14:39.920 --> 00:14:41.672
This is awesome!

00:14:41.672 --> 00:14:44.383
It's been a dream of mine
to do this in a big room.

00:14:44.383 --> 00:14:47.470
You're all in our way. Move it.

00:14:47.761 --> 00:14:50.806
Why are we all sleeping in
the same room again?

00:14:50.806 --> 00:14:52.766
That's how sleepovers work.

00:14:52.766 --> 00:14:55.269
It's a fascinating experience.

00:14:55.269 --> 00:14:57.062
Let's pick our spots.

00:14:57.062 --> 00:14:58.564
I'm here!

00:14:58.564 --> 00:15:00.733
Hey! That was my spot!

00:15:00.733 --> 00:15:02.776
I just want to sleep next to Kayo-chin!

00:15:03.319 --> 00:15:05.070
And you, Maki-chan?

00:15:06.822 --> 00:15:08.407
Doesn't matter.

00:15:09.492 --> 00:15:11.327
I'm turning off the lights.

00:15:11.327 --> 00:15:12.745
Okay.

00:15:20.753 --> 00:15:21.879
Hey.

00:15:23.631 --> 00:15:25.925
Hey, Kotori-chan.

00:15:27.009 --> 00:15:29.136
What's up, Honoka-chan?

00:15:29.136 --> 00:15:31.305
I can't sleep.

00:15:32.431 --> 00:15:35.518
Talking will only make it harder to fall asleep.

00:15:35.518 --> 00:15:37.436
Right, sorry.

00:15:37.436 --> 00:15:40.022
Look at Umi. She passed right out.

00:15:42.525 --> 00:15:46.070
Honoka-chan, you're a
heavy sleeper, aren't you?

00:15:46.070 --> 00:15:50.032
Yeah, but it feels like a waste to sleep tonight.

00:15:50.282 --> 00:15:52.493
We're all hanging out, y'know?

00:15:52.493 --> 00:15:56.539
Need I remind you that we didn't
come here solely to play?

00:15:56.539 --> 00:15:59.708
We'll be practicing hard in the
morning, so rest while you can.

00:16:00.084 --> 00:16:01.210
Okay.

00:16:02.503 --> 00:16:03.671
Maki-chan.

00:16:05.005 --> 00:16:06.090
Are you asleep?

00:16:07.132 --> 00:16:08.008
What?

00:16:08.384 --> 00:16:10.010
You really are just like her.

00:16:10.386 --> 00:16:12.638
Who...are you talking about?

00:16:18.894 --> 00:16:21.438
What was that noise?

00:16:21.438 --> 00:16:22.690
Not me!

00:16:22.690 --> 00:16:24.108
Or me.

00:16:24.108 --> 00:16:26.402
Will someone turn the lights back on?

00:16:31.740 --> 00:16:33.784
What are you doing, Honoka-chan?

00:16:33.784 --> 00:16:37.496
I thought I'd fall asleep faster
if I had a midnight snack.

00:16:37.496 --> 00:16:39.039
Jeez...

00:16:39.039 --> 00:16:41.750
Enough already.

00:16:43.002 --> 00:16:45.170
What's on your face?

00:16:45.170 --> 00:16:46.589
My beauty regimen.

00:16:46.589 --> 00:16:48.007
Khorosho...

00:16:48.382 --> 00:16:49.925
H-How horrifying...

00:16:50.884 --> 00:16:52.678
Who's "horrifying"!?

00:16:52.678 --> 00:16:54.930
Shut up and go to slee—!

00:16:55.848 --> 00:16:58.434
Maki-chan, why ever would you do that?

00:16:58.434 --> 00:17:00.102
Huh? Don't blame me.

00:17:00.811 --> 00:17:02.688
Why, you...!

00:17:02.688 --> 00:17:07.151
I know you want her to quiet down too,
but you shouldn't throw things like that.

00:17:07.735 --> 00:17:09.528
Ooh, what's this?

00:17:11.697 --> 00:17:13.490
All righty, then!

00:17:14.950 --> 00:17:17.202
You won't retaliate?

00:17:17.202 --> 00:17:18.704
You...

00:17:21.248 --> 00:17:22.583
Fine!

00:17:22.583 --> 00:17:25.252
If you're going to bring it, bring it.

00:17:49.443 --> 00:17:52.655
A-Are you okay?

00:17:53.947 --> 00:17:55.574
What do you think you're doing?

00:17:55.574 --> 00:17:58.160
U-Um...

00:18:03.540 --> 00:18:05.751
What is the meaning of this?

00:18:06.126 --> 00:18:09.421
I-1 didn't mean... I wasn't trying to hit you ...

00:18:09.755 --> 00:18:13.676
Yeah, yeah. We totally didn't mean to!

00:18:13.676 --> 00:18:18.764
Did I not tell you we would be
practicing first thing in the morning?

00:18:20.182 --> 00:18:20.641
Yep.

00:18:21.308 --> 00:18:23.852
And yet you act up in the middle of the night...

00:18:26.605 --> 00:18:28.732
Calm down, Umi.

00:18:28.732 --> 00:18:30.693
This won't end well for us.

00:18:30.693 --> 00:18:34.863
Umi-chan is really cranky if you wake her up.

00:18:37.491 --> 00:18:38.701
Nico-chan!

00:18:39.535 --> 00:18:42.329
It's no use. She's a lost cause!

00:18:42.329 --> 00:18:44.498
Supersonic pillow missiles...

00:18:44.498 --> 00:18:45.874
Khorosho...

00:18:47.960 --> 00:18:50.087
I pray that you're prepared.

00:18:50.629 --> 00:18:52.548
What're we gonna do, Honoka-chan?

00:18:52.548 --> 00:18:54.508
If we wanna live, we gotta fight!

00:18:55.884 --> 00:18:57.553
Forgive me, Umi!

00:18:58.512 --> 00:18:59.763
Rin-chan...

00:18:59.763 --> 00:19:01.640
Kayo-chin...

00:19:01.640 --> 00:19:04.518
Someone rescue us!

00:19:08.021 --> 00:19:09.106
Maki-chan.

00:19:09.106 --> 00:19:10.524
Nozomi-chan.

00:19:16.029 --> 00:19:17.448
Jeez...

00:19:17.781 --> 00:19:20.701
Sigh all you want, but you
started it, Maki-chan.

00:19:20.701 --> 00:19:24.121
N-No I didn't! That was Nozomi.

00:19:24.121 --> 00:19:26.290
I've no idea what you're talking about.

00:19:26.290 --> 00:19:27.499
You...!

00:19:27.499 --> 00:19:28.167
Hiya!

00:19:29.001 --> 00:19:30.627
Now what, Nozomi?

00:19:30.919 --> 00:19:34.256
Listen to how naturally
you're saying my name!

00:19:34.256 --> 00:19:35.466
What?

00:19:37.801 --> 00:19:39.678
What a little pain in the rear.

00:19:40.095 --> 00:19:44.475
I-I didn't ask you to do
anything like this for me!

00:20:21.678 --> 00:20:23.472
The early bird catches the worm.

00:20:23.847 --> 00:20:26.642
We should absorb some energy from the sun.

00:20:27.434 --> 00:20:29.061
Why are you doing this?

00:20:29.061 --> 00:20:31.438
It isn't for you or anything.

00:20:35.818 --> 00:20:37.569
The ocean is lovely, isn't it?

00:20:37.569 --> 00:20:42.449
Staring out at it makes you feel like
your worries are so insignificant.

00:20:44.493 --> 00:20:45.786
Hey, Maki-chan.

00:20:46.870 --> 00:20:50.415
I love all the members of J's.

00:20:51.416 --> 00:20:54.419
And I'd hate to see someone feel left out.

00:20:55.087 --> 00:20:58.882
Honoka-chan and her friends may
have originally formed y's,

00:20:58.882 --> 00:21:01.552
but I've kept my eyes on them all the while.

00:21:01.552 --> 00:21:04.888
I even advised them whenever
they met with resistance.

00:21:05.514 --> 00:21:08.141
That's how much I love them.

00:21:14.606 --> 00:21:17.234
Oh, maybe I said too much.

00:21:17.234 --> 00:21:18.694
Please keep it a secret.

00:21:21.864 --> 00:21:24.575
You're a real handful, aren't you?

00:21:25.617 --> 00:21:27.202
Your words, not mine.

00:21:27.202 --> 00:21:30.998
Maki-chan, Nozomi-chan!

00:21:30.998 --> 00:21:33.709
- Hey!
- Good morning!

00:21:55.480 --> 00:21:57.024
Hey, Eli?

00:22:01.695 --> 00:22:02.696
Thanks.

00:22:04.740 --> 00:22:05.949
Khorosho.

00:22:06.366 --> 00:22:12.331
Okay! Now let's do all we can
to prepare for Love Live!

00:22:12.331 --> 00:22:14.291
Yeah!

00:22:15.083 --> 00:22:20.797
Sunao ni oikakete yuukide oikakete Chase after
it with honesty, chase after it with courage.

00:22:20.797 --> 00:22:26.261
Chiisana negai ga ashita wo tsukuru That one
small wish is what will help to create tomorrow.

00:22:26.595 --> 00:22:32.684
Dekirukamo minna ga nozomunara It might
be possible if we all want it to come true.

00:22:32.684 --> 00:22:39.650
Dare yori ganbacchae tonikaku jounetsu no mama ni Give it
more effort than anyone else and stay as passionate as ever.

00:22:39.650 --> 00:22:44.696
Mezasu no wa kireina kaze fuku michi Let's aim to
find our path while riding on a beautiful wind.

00:22:45.614 --> 00:22:51.161
Hane no youni ude agete Spread your
arms out wide like they're your own wings.

00:22:51.161 --> 00:22:56.416
Mabushii mirai e to tobuyo We'll use
them to take off into our bright future.

00:22:57.626 --> 00:23:03.924
Kitto seishun ga kikoeru sono shunkan ni kikoeru You can hear the
songs filled with our youth, you can hear it in this one moment.

00:23:04.299 --> 00:23:09.554
Egao nara itsu no hi mo daijoubu As long as
we see you smiling, every day is worth it!

00:23:09.554 --> 00:23:15.978
Kitto seishun ga kikoeru sono shunkan ga mitaine You can hear the
songs filled with our youth, we want to see you at that moment.

00:23:15.978 --> 00:23:21.817
Tonari ni kimi ga ite (ureshii keshiki) I want you
to be right beside me. (It's such happy scenery.)

00:23:21.817 --> 00:23:27.239
Tonari wa kimi nanda
Only when the one right there is you.

00:23:35.831 --> 00:23:39.084
Next time on Love Live!
"The Greatest Concert"
